{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789751959,"nonce":"nrYgGPivaM3kj1pEOYFFK2CxUso=","title":"Interpreted call path costs ~8 us per call into native code","message":"HirInterpreter::call_by_id on the CallFn path clones the argument values into a Vec, looks the callee up in tick_callbacks, profile, shapes and module.functions (four hash lookups), ticks the bead through on_invoke, then call_native builds a word Vec and a NativeSig lookup for the thunk. nbody's main() (interpreted: called once, loop not resumable before the region repair) made 10 M such calls into native advance for 82 s against 0.7 s all-native. Per-function call sites should cache (shape, thunk, entry) in the CompiledFunction after the first call, keep a small-vector for words, and tick the bead through a cached Arc rather than a boxed FnMut lookup. Measure with ZYNTAX_TRACE_INTERP=1 counts on bench_nbody.","files":null}]}